course: dictionary
lesson: 12672
title: The word distinction
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A distinction is a clear difference between two things. It also means a high mark for excellent work, and being special or excellent. The clues are in the words around it. «There is a clear distinction between a cat and a rock: one is alive.» Here the sentence tells you the difference is about being alive.
explain: When a teacher says, «Mia passed her spelling test with distinction», she means Mia got a top mark. Pass with distinction means you did something very well, better than just passing.
explain: «The author is a writer of distinction.» This means the writer is special and excellent, and many people admire their work. Check the meaning by putting your own idea into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: A distinction is a clear difference between two things.
fact: A distinction can also be a high mark or grade for excellent work.
fact: «Make a distinction» means to see and show a clear difference between two things.
fact: «Pass with distinction» means to pass with a top grade.
fact: A «writer of distinction» is a special and excellent writer.
exercise: «A good reader can make a distinction between fact and opinion.» What does make a distinction mean? | To forget about it | To read very slowly | To copy the words | *To see and show a clear difference
exercise: «Mia got a distinction in her maths test.» What does distinction mean here? | A kind of sum | A plain blue cover | *A top mark for excellent work | A mark for a wrong answer
exercise: «Ms Patel is a writer of distinction.» What does distinction mean here? | *Being special and excellent | Being in the wrong place | A type of pencil | A small spot on the page
test: «There is a clear distinction between a cat and a rock: one is alive.» What is a distinction in this sentence? | A kind of picture | A very long sentence | A question for the teacher | *A clear difference between two things
test: «Sam hopes to pass the exam with distinction.» What does with distinction mean? | Without any help at all | Late, after everyone else | With a broken pencil | *With a top grade for excellent work
exam: Which phrase means to show a clear difference between two things? | in distinction to nothing | pass with distinction | *make a distinction | a writer of distinction
